{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.BindingAlphaShiftExtension","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.BindingAlphaShiftExtension","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Cast.Defs"],"declarations":17,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.lightNucleiForceCarrierKnot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.lightNucleiForceCarrierKnot","kind":"instance","line":247,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/binding-alpha-shift-extension.lean#L247-L261","doc":"**Concrete `BindingForceCarrierKnot` instance covering all four\nlight-nuclei candidates A ∈ {2, 3, 4}.**\n\nCloses the Phase-3 candidate identifications in a single\ninstance.  Since `lightNucleusAlphaShift` is defined directly\nas `bindingAlphaShift ∘ ⟨lightNucleusP, lightNucleusK⟩`,\n`matches_alpha_shift` holds **definitionally** — the proof is\n`rfl`.  **No** `sorry`.\n\nSubstrate-uniqueness of each `(p_A, k_A)` — proving these are\nthe substrate's choices rather than candidates — remains open\npending the H_{3A}(q) Wedderburn-block minimisation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.light_nucleus_alpha_shift_at_He4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.light_nucleus_alpha_shift_at_He4","kind":"theorem","line":243,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/binding-alpha-shift-extension.lean#L243-L245","doc":"Sanity check at ⁴He's candidate T(3, 4): α_shift = 8. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.light_nucleus_alpha_shift_at_A3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.light_nucleus_alpha_shift_at_A3","kind":"theorem","line":239,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/binding-alpha-shift-extension.lean#L239-L241","doc":"Sanity check at the A = 3 mirror pair T(2, 5): α_shift = 5. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.light_nucleus_alpha_shift_at_deuteron","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.light_nucleus_alpha_shift_at_deuteron","kind":"theorem","line":235,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/binding-alpha-shift-extension.lean#L235-L237","doc":"Sanity check at the deuteron candidate T(2, 3): α_shift = 3. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.lightNucleusAlphaShift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.lightNucleusAlphaShift","kind":"def","line":225,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/binding-alpha-shift-extension.lean#L225-L233","doc":"Light-nuclei α_shift profile, defined directly as\n`bindingAlphaShift (lightNucleusP A) (lightNucleusK A)`.\n\nUsing the structural composition rather than re-listing the\nmagic values (3, 5, 8) eliminates duplication and lets all\ndownstream proofs close definitionally (`rfl`).  Per Gemini\nmedium-priority review on #1485. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.lightNucleusK","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.lightNucleusK","kind":"def","line":217,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/binding-alpha-shift-extension.lean#L217-L223","doc":"Light-nuclei force-carrier `k`-index selector.  A=2 → 3 (T(2,3));\nA=3 → 5 (T(2,5)); A=4 → 4 (T(3,4)).  Sentinel `0` elsewhere. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.lightNucleusP","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.lightNucleusP","kind":"def","line":208,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/binding-alpha-shift-extension.lean#L208-L215","doc":"Light-nuclei force-carrier `p`-index selector at A ∈ {2, 3, 4}.\nA=2 → 2 (T(2,3)); A=3 → 2 (T(2,5)); A=4 → 3 (T(3,4)).  Sentinel\n`0` elsewhere. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.binding_subsingleton","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.binding_subsingleton","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/binding-alpha-shift-extension.lean#L146-L162","doc":"**Sub-singleton companion.**  The space of binding evaluators\nsharing the same `(m_e, ρ_0)` and a common\n`BindingForceCarrierKnot` identification `(p, k)` is a\nsubsingleton.  Refactored 2026-05-30 per the same #1464 review\nto consume the force-carrier class rather than an ad-hoc\nequality. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.binding_unique_via_alpha_shift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.binding_unique_via_alpha_shift","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/binding-alpha-shift-extension.lean#L119-L144","doc":"**Binding uniqueness theorem (via α_shift).**  Given the\nper-rep Reeb phase axiom + the force-carrier knot identification,\ntwo binding evaluators sharing the same substrate parameters\n(m_e, ρ_0, knot identification) agree pointwise.\n\nPer AGENTS.md §3b-cond: sorry-free conditional on the two\nclasses.  Phase 3 (the actual `(p_A, k_A)` identification) is\nresearch-grade and deferred.\n\n**Refactored 2026-05-30 per @litlfred review** (#1464 line-129\ncomment): the theorem now derives the `αShiftAt` equality from\nthe shared `BindingForceCarrierKnot` class via\n`matches_alpha_shift`, eliminating the ad-hoc hypothesis and\naligning the Lean structure with the audit's §3b-cond gating\nintent. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:binding-alpha-shift-extension","label":"prop:binding-alpha-shift-extension","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/binding-alpha-shift-extension.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BindingForceCarrierKnot.matches_alpha_shift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BindingForceCarrierKnot.matches_alpha_shift","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/binding-alpha-shift-extension.lean#L117-L117","doc":"For every nucleus A, the per-rep α_shift equals the formal\nvalue at the identified torus knot. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BindingForceCarrierKnot.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BindingForceCarrierKnot.mk","kind":"ctor","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/binding-alpha-shift-extension.lean#L113-L113","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BindingForceCarrierKnot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BindingForceCarrierKnot","kind":"class","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/binding-alpha-shift-extension.lean#L104-L117","doc":"**Force-carrier knot identification class.**  The substrate\nfixes a torus knot `T(p_A, k_A)` per nucleus A such that\n`αShiftAt A = bindingAlphaShift p_A k_A = k_A · (p_A − 1)`.\n\nPhase 3 open math: the identification (`p_A`, `k_A`) for each\nA ∈ {2, 3, 4, ...} must be derived from the substrate's\nHecke-Wedderburn block structure on H_{3A}(q) at the binding's\nminimum-dimensional non-trivial irrep, analogous to the meson\nforce-carrier pair derivation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BindingPerRepReebPhase.factors","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BindingPerRepReebPhase.factors","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/binding-alpha-shift-extension.lean#L102-L102","doc":"B(A) = m_e · ρ_0 · (αShiftAt A : R).  Substrate identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BindingPerRepReebPhase.αShiftAt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BindingPerRepReebPhase.αShiftAt","kind":"def","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/binding-alpha-shift-extension.lean#L100-L100","doc":"B(A) factors through α_shift at the binding-specific torus\nknot.  The function `αShiftAt` records, per nucleus index A,\nthe proved α_shift value `k_A · (p_A − 1)` of the substrate-\nidentified force-carrier torus knot `T(p_A, k_A)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BindingPerRepReebPhase.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BindingPerRepReebPhase.mk","kind":"ctor","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/binding-alpha-shift-extension.lean#L94-L94","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BindingPerRepReebPhase","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BindingPerRepReebPhase","kind":"class","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/binding-alpha-shift-extension.lean#L83-L102","doc":"**Binding per-rep Reeb phase class.**  For each light nucleus\n`A`, the binding energy `B(A)` scales as `m_e · ρ_0 · α_shift_K`\nwhere `α_shift_K` is the pole order of σ on the column-rich\nirrep of the binding-specific force-carrier torus knot\n`T(p_K, k_K)`, and `ρ_0` is the substrate-universal per-rep\nReeb coupling pinned by the deuteron (≈ 14.7 MeV/rad per\n`binding_rotation_phase_lead.py`).\n\nPer AGENTS.md §3b-cond: the binding closure is gated on the\n**per-rep Reeb phase axiom** (substrate identity) and the\n**force-carrier knot identification** (Phase 3 open math).  ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.bindingAlphaShift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.bindingAlphaShift","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/binding-alpha-shift-extension.lean#L65-L68","doc":"α_shift formula (local mirror of\n`mass-theory/alpha-shift-torus-knot.alphaShift` for ergonomics).\nPole order of σ on the column-rich irrep of T(p, k). ","signatureChunk":0}]}